Exercise 1 * :

Prove that the set of all formulas of propositional logic is denumerable.

We must show that of all formulas containing all variables and of all degrees is a denumerable set. Starting with only one variable p, we can create a finite set of formulae by simply taking all the formulas of degree 1 with p. Then, adding in another variable q, we can get all the formulae of length two by simply connecting a formula in the first set q. Because there are only a finite number of connectives, and there are only a finite number of formulae in the first set, the number of formulae in q will also be finite. Because continuing this pattern obtains all possible formulas, and it goes on for ever (as there are an infinite number of possible propositional variables), the set of all of the formulae can be put into a 1-1 correspondence with the set of all natural numbers. 

